  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Kiyari began as work chants for hauling timber and stone, setting the pull of a crew to a leader's call, and in Edo the tobi construction workers and town firemen made them ceremonial songs for festivals, building rites and the New Year fire-brigade parade. Edo kiyari is kept in Tokyo by the Edo Shōbō Kinenkai, the preservation society of the old fire brigades.",
